---
title: Salted chocolate chip cookies
servings: 18
yield: about 18 cookies
tags: [vegan, dairy-free, make-ahead]
source: Salted Chocolate Chip Cookies (Secretly Vegan) by Ovenly, https://www.oven.ly/recipes/project-two-llrgk-typsa
---

In a #large bowl{}, whisk the @all-purpose flour{250%g}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, @baking soda{3/4%tsp} and @salt{1/2%tsp}. Toss the @dark chocolate chips{1 1/4%cup} through it.

In a second #large bowl{}, whisk the @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}, @light brown sugar{1/2%cup}(packed, lumps broken up), @canola oil{1/2%cup}(plus 1 tbsp) and @water{1/4%cup}(plus 1 tbsp) for ~{2%minutes}, until smooth.

Stir the dry mix into the wet with a spatula just until no flour shows. Cover and chill at least ~{12%hours} and up to 24 hours.

> The long chill is what makes these work; don't skip it.

Heat the oven to 350°F and line two rimmed #sheet pans{} with parchment. Scoop the dough into 2-inch mounds. Freezing them ~{10%minutes} helps them keep their shape.

Sprinkle with @flaked sea salt{} and bake ~{12%minutes} to 13 minutes, until just golden at the edges. Cool completely.
